# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paths where a mistake is expensive or irreversible. Listed separately from
# the `lib/` catch-all so the reason is visible, and so an owner can be split
# off later without hunting for which rule applied.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Schema and migrations. A wrong migration destroys a user's data, and unlike
# a bad widget it cannot be fixed by the next release -- the rows are gone.
lib/data/local/         @ajay99511

# Alarm and notification platform code. Everything here fails *silently*: an
# alarm that does not arrive looks identical to one that was never set.
lib/core/services/      @ajay99511

# Android build and manifest. Holds the release signing config, the declared
# permissions, and the applicationId -- which is permanent once published.
android/                @ajay99511

# Decision records. These are the project's memory of why things are the way
# they are; a silent edit is worse than no record.
docs/decisions/         @ajay99511

# CI and repository automation. The checks are the only thing standing between
# the default branch and an unverified change.
.github/                @ajay99511
